ONEDRAFT
CAD-AI — Aria Powered
Configuration, Secrets & Environment Management
Version 1.0
Status: Implementation Specification
System: OneDraft
Configuration Layer: Centralized, Environment-Aware
Secrets Layer: Secure Secret Management
Runtime Model: Immutable Configuration at Process Start
Deployment Model: Environment-Separated
Primary Environments: Development / Test / Staging / Production

1. CONFIGURATION DESIGN PRINCIPLE
OneDraft shall treat configuration as a controlled system resource rather than as arbitrary application state.
Configuration determines how the OneDraft runtime behaves within a particular environment.
The configuration system shall provide:
Environment separation
Configuration hierarchy
Secret isolation
Runtime configuration
Deployment configuration
Feature configuration
Service configuration
External provider configuration
Security configuration
Operational configuration
Configuration must be deterministic, auditable and reproducible.

2. CONFIGURATION AND SECRETS SEPARATION
Configuration and secrets are separate architectural concepts.
Configuration may contain:
environment
service endpoints
feature flags
queue names
database hostnames
storage locations
logging levels
timeouts
worker limits
API limits
model configuration
drawing defaults
Secrets may contain:
database passwords
API keys
signing keys
JWT secrets
OAuth credentials
encryption keys
provider credentials
webhook secrets
service credentials
Secrets must never be committed to the source repository.

3. ENVIRONMENT MODEL
OneDraft shall initially define:
development
test
staging
production
Each environment shall have its own configuration boundary.
Conceptually:
OneDraft
    ↓
Environment
    ↓
Configuration
    ↓
Services
    ↓
Workers
    ↓
External Dependencies
Production configuration must never be implicitly inherited from development configuration.

