34. CONFIGURATION VERSIONS
Significant configuration changes shall be versionable.
A configuration record should identify:
configuration_version
environment
created_at
created_by
change_reason
configuration_hash
This permits reconstruction of runtime conditions.

35. CONFIGURATION HASHING
A normalized configuration representation may be hashed.
Example:
configuration_hash
The hash provides an integrity identifier for the effective configuration state.
Secrets themselves must not be included in plaintext within the hash record.

36. IMMUTABLE DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATION
A deployed application instance should operate from a known configuration snapshot.
Conceptually:
DEPLOYMENT
    ↓
CONFIGURATION SNAPSHOT
    ↓
APPLICATION INSTANCE
Configuration changes should normally produce a new deployment or controlled runtime configuration update.

37. RUNTIME CONFIGURATION
Runtime configuration may be changed without restarting a service only where explicitly supported.
Examples may include:
feature flags
operational thresholds
non-secret tuning values
maintenance mode
Security-sensitive configuration should require controlled deployment or restart.

38. CONFIGURATION RELOAD
Services supporting configuration reload shall expose an internal mechanism.
Conceptually:
CONFIGURATION CHANGE
        ↓
VALIDATE
        ↓
LOAD
        ↓
APPLY
        ↓
HEALTH CHECK
An invalid configuration must not replace the currently valid configuration.

39. CONFIGURATION ATOMICITY
Configuration updates shall be atomic.
The system must not enter a state where only part of a configuration update has been applied.
Conceptually:
OLD CONFIG
    ↓
VALIDATE NEW CONFIG
    ↓
APPLY NEW CONFIG
    ↓
NEW CONFIG
If validation fails:
OLD CONFIG REMAINS ACTIVE

40. CONFIGURATION SCHEMA VALIDATION
Configuration shall be validated for:
type
required fields
allowed values
ranges
relationships
environment restrictions
secret references
dependency availability
Invalid values shall prevent startup or configuration activation.

41. ENVIRONMENT-SPECIFIC RESTRICTIONS
Certain configuration values shall be restricted by environment.
Example:
production
    ↓
production database only

staging
    ↓
staging database only

test
