81. CONFIGURATION DRIFT
The system shall detect unexpected differences between declared and deployed configuration.
Conceptually:
DECLARED CONFIG
       ↓
COMPARE
       ↓
DEPLOYED CONFIG
       ↓
DRIFT RESULT
Drift should generate an operational event.

82. CONFIGURATION DRIFT RESPONSE
Configuration drift may result in:
WARNING
BLOCKED DEPLOYMENT
AUTOMATIC RECONCILIATION
OPERATOR REVIEW
The selected behavior shall depend on configuration criticality.
Security configuration should receive the highest protection.

